---
import Layout from '../layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Thadeus Smith"
  description="Résumé of Thadeus Smith: Director of Education at Lumos Debate, speech and debate coach, editor at Champion Briefs, and Wikipedia administrator."
>
<style>
.section{
border-left: 6px solid;
padding-left: 0.5rem;
}
.resume{
display: flex;
flex-wrap:wrap;
justify-content: space-between;
margin: 0 0 2rem ;
padding: 0.25rem;
}
.position{
font-weight: 650;
padding: 0.1em 0;
flex-basis: 100%;
border-bottom: 3px solid black;
}
.date{
padding: 0.1em 0;
flex-shrink: 0;
flex-basis: 40%;
text-align: right;
}
.company{
padding: 0.1em 0;
flex-basis: 50%;
flex-grow: 1;
flex-shrink: 1;
margin-right: 1em;
}
.description{
flex-basis: 100%;
font-size: 85%;
opacity: 70%;
margin-top: 0.5rem;
}

@media screen and (max-width: 800px) {
  .section{
    border-left: 4px solid;
    padding-left: 0.25rem;
  }
}
</style>
<main id="main">
<div class="section">
<h2>Experience</h2>

<p class="resume"><span class="position">Director of Education</span><br>
<span class="company">Lumos Debate</span> <span class="date">June 2026–Present</span>
<span class="description">
Lumos Debate is the leading provider of speech and debate education in the Boston and New York metro areas, running workshops and classes that serve hundreds of students annually.
<br>
• Supervise and train dozens of instructors teaching small-group Public Forum Debate classes, providing instructional coaching and stepping in as a substitute when needed
<br>
• Oversee enrollment, staffing, and family communications for weekly classes at multiple Massachusetts locations
<br>
• Lead growth efforts, including open houses and trial workshops, to expand access to speech and debate education in Greater Boston
<br>
• Organize monthly virtual tournaments that give hundreds of students feedback on argumentation and presentation
</span>
</p>

<p class="resume"><span class="position">External Coach</span><br>
<span class="company">American Heritage Schools</span> <span class="date">June 2026–Present</span>
<span class="description">
• Continue coaching Congressional Debate and World Schools Debate competitors remotely and at national circuit tournaments following my move to Boston
</span>
</p>

<p class="resume"><span class="position">Speech and Debate Teacher</span><br>
<span class="company">American Heritage Schools</span> <span class="date">June 2023–June 2026</span>
<span class="description">
American Heritage School (Broward) runs one of the top-ranked speech and debate programs in the country. The program won the Florida State Championship every year from 2020 to 2026 and produced 26 national qualifiers and 29 Tournament of Champions bids in the 2024–25 season.
<br>
• Led the Congressional Debate team, which in the 2025–26 season included the Florida State Runner-Up, the Champion Presiding Officer at the Tournament of Champions, and the 9th-place finisher in the Senate at the National Speech and Debate Tournament
<br>
• Coached the 2025–26 Florida State Champion and NIETOC Champion in Impromptu Speaking
<br>
• Taught speech and debate classes from grades 5 through 12, designing full-year curricula for Congressional Debate and Extemporaneous Speaking and half-year curricula for World Schools Debate and Big Questions Debate
<br>
• Managed tournament registration and logistics, including parent judge rotations and family information meetings
</span>
</p>

<p class="resume"><span class="position">Content Editor</span><br>
<span class="company">Champion Briefs</span> <span class="date">July 2024–Present</span>
<span class="description">
• Serve as lead editor for the monthly Public Forum Debate brief, reviewing research contributions from a team of coaches to ensure argumentative rigor and source integrity
</span>
</p>

<p class="resume"><span class="position">Researcher</span><br>
<span class="company">Champion Briefs</span> <span class="date">July 2023–July 2024</span>
<span class="description">
• Conducted topic research and organized evidence on upcoming debate topics, ranging from domestic political issues such as executive orders to international subjects like the European Union
</span>
</p>

<p class="resume"><span class="position">DEI and Community Planning Coordinator</span><br>
<span class="company">Kitsap County Commissioner's Office</span> <span class="date">June 2022–July 2023</span>
<span class="description">
One of 35 people selected for the Lead for America National Hometown Fellowship, an AmeriCorps program that places young professionals in public service roles in their hometown communities.
<br>
• Conducted a year-long listening tour, interviewing over 150 county stakeholders to understand their needs and creating a report for the County Commissioners
<br>
• Spearheaded research into equity issues around the county, including a survey of 1,100 staff members, that culminated in the creation of the county's first full-time DEI Manager position
<br>
• Facilitated community forums and advised commissioners on organizational planning and diverse hiring pipelines
</span>
</p>

<p class="resume"><span class="position">Content Manager</span><br>
<span class="company">TalkMaze</span> <span class="date">April 2020–June 2022</span>
<span class="description">
Founding team member of TalkMaze, an education startup providing online speech and debate education and competition opportunities to schools without the resources for classroom-based teams.
<br>
• Led a team of two dozen coaches from around the world to develop a standardized, culturally responsive curriculum taught to thousands of students across three continents
<br>
• Developed a series of on-demand video courses covering multiple speech and debate events, increasing accessibility and student retention
</span>
</p>

<p class="resume"><span class="position">Overtime Session Field Organizer Intern</span><br>
<span class="company">Civic Ventures</span> <span class="date">January 2020</span>
<span class="description">
One of two interns at Civic Ventures, which advocates for progressive policy changes in the Pacific Northwest.
<br>
• Presented information on the "Restore Our Time" campaign to dozens of local political party meetings in the Seattle metro area
<br>
• Delivered thousands of constituent notecards to Washington legislators, resulting in Washington adopting the strongest overtime protections in the nation
</span>
</p>
</div>

